(18592, 62, 'Artisan Vapor Company', 'avldispensary@gmail.com', 'https://warezok.net/user/oddycbd3448/', '94.155.33.88', '2021-06-11 18:09:26', '2021-06-11 22:09:26', 'I operate a vape store submission site and we have had a listing from a vape store in the USA that also sells CBD product lines. A Month afterwards, PayPal has written to use to say that our account has been restricted and have asked us to remove PayPal as a payment solution from our vape store directory. We do not retail CBD items such as CBD oil. We simply offer advertising and marketing solutions to CBD companies. I have checked out Holland &amp; Barrett-- the UK\'s Reputable Wellness Retail store and if you take a good look, you will see that they supply a fairly considerable series of CBD goods, particularly CBD oil and they also happen to take PayPal as a payment method. It appears that PayPal is applying double standards to different companies. Due to this limitation, I can no longer take PayPal on my CBD-related online site. This has limited my payment choices and now, I am seriously dependent on Cryptocurrency payments and direct bank transfers. I have gotten in touch with a solicitor from a Magic Circle law practice in London and they stated that what PayPal is undertaking is definitely unlawful and inequitable as it should be applying a systematic standard to all companies. I am yet to seek advice from one more legal representative from a US law office in London to see what PayPal\'s legal position is in the United States. For the time being, I would be highly appreciative if anyone here at targetdomain could offer me with alternative payment processors/merchants that work with CBD firms.', 0, '0', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/62.0.3202.94 Safari/537.36', '', 0, 0),
