(188, 3, '2014-06-03 03:31:59', '2014-06-03 03:31:59', '<a href=\"http://fullmooncentral.com/\"><img class=\"size-medium wp-image-121 aligncenter\" alt=\"indx_logo2bed1210\" src=\"http://scottyandallie.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/05/indx_logo2bed1210-300x146.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"146\" /></a>\n\nWe are SO EXCITED. Our wedding weekend will be Friday, June 5th through  Sunday, June 7th of 2015. \n\nThe location is <a href=\"http://www.fullmoonresort.com/\">Full Moon Resort</a> in Big Indian, NY.\n\nIt\'s going to be an awesome three day festival of family, friends, music, nature and love. Full Moon Resort is 20 minutes from Woodstock. It\'s on the top of a mountain so there\'s no cell phone service.\n\nMore details coming. Save the date!\n\n-Allie &amp; Scott', 'We have a date and a venue!', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', '107-autosave-v1', '', '', '2014-06-03 03:31:59', '2014-06-03 03:31:59', '', 107, 'http://scottyandallie.com/2014/06/03/107-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(189, 3, '2014-06-03 03:34:15', '2014-06-03 03:34:15', '', '10173819_10104437583478983_435875586873191237_n', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', '10173819_10104437583478983_435875586873191237_n', '', '', '2014-06-03 03:34:15', '2014-06-03 03:34:15', '', 122, 'http://scottyandallie.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/10173819_10104437583478983_435875586873191237_n.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(192, 3, '2015-01-29 08:54:35', '2015-01-29 08:54:35', 'Our wedding will take place at <strong><a href=\"http://fullmooncentral.com\">Full Moon Resort</a></strong> in the the “Forever Wild” Catskill Forest Preserve in upstate New York. Dedicated to the celebration of nature, music and the arts, this one hundred-acre wonderland of mountains, fields, and streams is a world of its own. Full Moon is located in the mountains of the Hudson Valley, 30 minutes west of Woodstock, 2.5 hours from NYC.\n\nValley View Road\nBig Indian, NY 12410\nTel: (845) 254-5117\nwww.fullmoonresort.com\n\nClick to explore a map of the grounds.\n\n<a href=\"http://scottyandallie.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/full-moon.png\"><img class=\"alignleft size-full wp-image-228\" src=\"http://scottyandallie.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/full-moon.png\" alt=\"full-moon\" width=\"600\" height=\"884\" /></a>', 'Full Moon Resort', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', '117-autosave-v1', '', '', '2015-01-29 08:54:35', '2015-01-29 08:54:35', '', 117, 'http://scottyandallie.com/2014/08/07/117-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(193, 3, '2014-08-07 03:18:39', '2014-08-07 03:18:39', '<strong>FRIDAY</strong>\r\n3pm — Guest checkin and snacks at Valley View House, lawn games, swimming, hanging.\r\n7pm — Welcome BBQ in the Barn/Toasts and Roasts (Attire: Country chic/cocktail casual - sundress, Hawaiian shirts, jeans okay, etc)\r\n9pm —  Live Yacht Rock in the Barn with AMGold\r\n9pm — Campfire all night\r\n1am — Afterparty in the Billiards Room\r\n\r\n<strong>SATURDAY</strong>\r\n8:30–10:30am — Allie\'s Hangover Breakfast in the Cafe\r\n12:30pm-2pm — Scotty\'s Taco Bar Lunch in the Barn\r\n2pm — Kickball Game and Wiffle Ball Game in the Middle Field\r\n5pm — We get married in the Lower Grove! (Attire: Formal)\r\n6:00pm — Cocktail Hour on the Front Lawn\r\n7:00-11:00pm — PARTY! In the Reception Tent with Eturnity Band\r\n11:00pm - Sparkler parade to the After Party Jam at the Performance Space Bar With DJ Milky Manchester - bring your musical instruments or talents\r\n2:00am — After-After Party in the Billiards Room\r\n\r\nSunday\r\n8:30am-10:30am — Farewell brunch in the Cafe\r\n11am — Checkout\r\n\r\n**For friends and family staying in NYC on Sunday night, you\'re welcome to come to our apartment in Brooklyn for a rooftop hang anytime after 6PM.\r\n\r\nThe Full Moon pool is open daily from dawn to dusk.', 'Itinerary', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'itinerary', '', '', '2015-06-01 20:35:44', '2015-06-01 20:35:44', '', 0, 'http://scottyandallie.com/?page_id=193', 0, 'page', '', 0),
(194, 3, '2014-08-07 03:19:07', '2014-08-07 03:19:07', ' ', '', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', '194', '', '', '2015-06-01 20:36:11', '2015-06-01 20:36:11', '', 0, 'http://scottyandallie.com/?p=194', 2, 'nav_menu_item', '', 0),
(195, 3, '2014-08-07 03:22:11', '2014-08-07 03:22:11', '<strong>1. What time should I arrive? Where am I going?</strong>\r\n\r\nYou can start checking into your room at Full Moon at the main area (Valley View house) starting at 3PM on Friday, June 5. We will be vibing at Valley View from 3-6PM with snacks &amp; music. Then the first official event is the BBQ at 7PM.\r\n\r\nThe weekend itinerary is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"http://scottyandallie.com/itinerary/\">here</a></span>. Directions <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"http://scottyandallie.com/driving-directions/\">here</a></span>. Be sure to give yourself at least 3 hours to drive from NY/NJ -- there is a ton of traffic on Fridays.\r\n\r\nFor folks staying off-site at Alpine Inn, you can check in as early as 1PM. After you checkin at Alpine, please come join us at Full Moon.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. What should I bring? What should I wear?</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Casual cocktail attire for Friday\'s 7PM BBQ. What you\'d wear to a nice dinner, like a sundress for women. Jeans, shorts (or jorts) are fine, too.</li>\r\n	<li>Formal attire for Saturday\'s 5PM wedding ceremony and reception. Suit or tux for men, and cocktail dress or gown for women.</li>\r\n	<li>Swimsuit, flip flops and beach towel for the pool.</li>\r\n	<li>Jacket or sweater - it gets cold at night in the 50\'s.</li>\r\n	<li>Bathrobe/slippers <i>(some guest rooms have shared baths or hall baths)</i></li>\r\n	<li>Hairdryer</li>\r\n	<li>Flashlight</li>\r\n	<li>Umbrella</li>\r\n	<li>Cash for the bar at the after-parties on Friday &amp; Saturday nights -- the bar does not take credit cards and there is no ATM for 20 miles.</li>\r\n	<li>Musical instruments, if you\'d like to play around the campfire or jam at the after parties</li>\r\n	<li>If you\'d like to explore hiking trails, bring boots or sneakers.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>3. What does Full Moon provide for guests?</strong>\r\n\r\nFull Moon is a rustic lodging facility, not a hotel, but it\'s quaint, clean and provides:\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Bath towels &amp; bed linens</li>\r\n	<li>Shampoo, conditioner, soap</li>\r\n	<li>Ice</li>\r\n	<li>Complimentary teas and coffee at Valley View from the time breakfast is served until the last meal of the day is served</li>\r\n	<li>Front desk has emergency and basic medical equipment (bandaids, tylenol, etc). Closest pharmacy is approximately 20 minutes from Full Moon.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>4. What\'s the weather like?</strong>\r\n\r\nNestled in the Catskill Mountains, it will be in the 70\'s - 80\'s F. At night it gets down to the 50\'s F.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Is there cell phone reception?</strong>\r\n\r\nThere is no cell phone reception at Full Moon Resort or in the forest preserve but <strong><em>there is free WiFi so you can still send and receive texts and emails</em></strong>. Also, complimentary landline phone service is available at all times at Valley View.\r\n\r\n<strong>6. Can I bring my own alcohol?</strong>\r\n\r\nYou can bring your own cooler and alcohol for use in your room.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>7. How can guests be reached at Full Moon?</strong>\r\n\r\nPlease call the front desk at Full Moon at (845) 254 - 5117.\r\n\r\n<strong>8. </strong><strong>My question isn\'t here.</strong>\r\n\r\nPlease email allie.feldman@gmail.com or call us: Allie 908-370-2689 and Scotty 646-715-7347.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'FAQ', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'faq', '', '', '2015-06-05 04:34:33', '2015-06-05 04:34:33', '', 0, 'http://scottyandallie.com/?page_id=195', 0, 'page', '', 0),
