(245, 2, '2015-01-31 06:09:48', '2015-01-31 06:09:48', 'We just filmed an episode of Say Yes To The Dress at the one and only Kleinfeld\'s. Did we say yes to the dress? Watch for the episode in Spring 2015 to find out...\n\n&nbsp;', 'Say Yes To The Dress!', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', '206-autosave-v1', '', '', '2015-01-31 06:09:48', '2015-01-31 06:09:48', '', 206, 'http://scottyandallie.com/2015/01/31/206-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(247, 2, '2015-01-10 06:40:58', '2015-01-10 06:40:58', 'Scotty\'s bachelor party will be in New Orleans. Allie\'s bachelorette party will be in Las Vegas.', '#Feyonce', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', 'feyonce-2', '', '', '2015-01-31 06:53:46', '2015-01-31 06:53:46', '', 0, 'http://scottyandallie.com/?p=247', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(248, 2, '2015-06-05 04:34:08', '2015-06-05 04:34:08', '<strong>1. What time should I arrive? Where am I going?</strong>\n\nYou can start checking into your room at Full Moon at the main area (Valley View house) starting at 3PM on Friday, June 5. We will be vibing at Valley View from 3-6PM with snacks &amp; music. Then the first official event is the BBQ at 7PM.\n\nThe weekend itinerary is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"http://scottyandallie.com/itinerary/\">here</a></span>. Directions <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"http://scottyandallie.com/driving-directions/\">here</a></span>. Be sure to give yourself at least 3 hours to drive from NY/NJ -- there is a ton of traffic on Fridays.\n\nFor folks staying off-site at Alpine Inn, you can check in as early as 1PM. After you checkin at Alpine, please come join us at Full Moon.\n\n<strong>2. What should I bring? What should I wear?</strong>\n<ul>\n	<li>Casual cocktail attire for Friday\'s 7PM BBQ and Yacht Rock party. What you\'d wear to a nice dinner, like a sundress for women. Jeans, shorts (or jorts) are fine, too.</li>\n	<li>Formal attire for Saturday\'s 5PM wedding ceremony and reception. Suit or tux for men, and cocktail dress or gown for women.</li>\n	<li>Swimsuit, flip flops and beach towel for the pool.</li>\n	<li>Jacket or sweater - it gets cold at night in the 50\'s.</li>\n	<li>Bathrobe/slippers <i>(some guest rooms have shared baths or hall baths)</i></li>\n	<li>Hairdryer</li>\n	<li>Flashlight</li>\n	<li>Umbrella</li>\n	<li>Cash for the bar at the after-parties on Friday &amp; Saturday nights -- the bar does not take credit cards and there is no ATM for 20 miles.</li>\n	<li>Musical instruments, if you\'d like to play around the campfire or jam at the after parties</li>\n	<li>If you\'d like to explore hiking trails, bring boots or sneakers.</li>\n</ul>\n<strong>3. What does Full Moon provide for guests?</strong>\n\nFull Moon is a rustic lodging facility, not a hotel, but it\'s quaint, clean and provides:\n<ul>\n	<li>Bath towels &amp; bed linens</li>\n	<li>Shampoo, conditioner, soap</li>\n	<li>Ice</li>\n	<li>Complimentary teas and coffee at Valley View from the time breakfast is served until the last meal of the day is served</li>\n	<li>Front desk has emergency and basic medical equipment (bandaids, tylenol, etc). Closest pharmacy is approximately 20 minutes from Full Moon.</li>\n</ul>\n&nbsp;\n\n<strong>4. What\'s the weather like?</strong>\n\nNestled in the Catskill Mountains, it will be in the 70\'s - 80\'s F. At night it gets down to the 50\'s F.\n\n<strong>5. Is there cell phone reception?</strong>\n\nThere is no cell phone reception at Full Moon Resort or in the forest preserve but <strong><em>there is free WiFi so you can still send and receive texts and emails</em></strong>. Also, complimentary landline phone service is available at all times at Valley View.\n\n<strong>6. Can I bring my own alcohol?</strong>\n\nYou can bring your own cooler and alcohol for use in your room.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<strong>7. How can guests be reached at Full Moon?</strong>\n\nPlease call the front desk at Full Moon at (845) 254 - 5117.\n\n<strong>8. </strong><strong>My question isn\'t here.</strong>\n\nPlease email allie.feldman@gmail.com or call us: Allie 908-370-2689 and Scotty 646-715-7347.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;', 'FAQ', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', '195-autosave-v1', '', '', '2015-06-05 04:34:08', '2015-06-05 04:34:08', '', 195, 'http://scottyandallie.com/2015/01/31/195-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(249, 2, '2015-01-31 22:26:45', '2015-01-31 22:26:45', 'The bridal shower is scheduled for Sunday, March 1st at noon at Allie\'s childhood home in Westfield, New Jersey. <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><a href=\"http://rsvpwpd.com/allief\">Kindly RSVP here</a></strong></span>.\n\nThis is also the last time to party at 420 -- the house we all loved for over 22 years is officially going to closing the very next day.\n\n<a href=\"http://scottyandallie.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/Shower.jpg\"><img class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-231\" src=\"http://scottyandallie.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/Shower-221x300.jpg\" alt=\"Shower\" width=\"221\" height=\"300\" /></a>\n\n', 'Bridal Shower', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', '230-autosave-v1', '', '', '2015-01-31 22:26:45', '2015-01-31 22:26:45', '', 230, 'http://scottyandallie.com/2015/01/31/230-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
