(254, 3, '2015-02-03 19:17:01', '2015-02-03 19:17:01', '<p class=\"p1\">Our wedding is a 3-day festival, from Friday afternoon (June 5) until breakfast on Sunday (June 7) at <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><a href=\"http://scottyandallie.com/full-moon-resort/\">Full Moon Resort</a></strong></span>. All guests will be staying in cottages at Full Moon, which provides accommodations and meals at very reasonable rates. We\'ll be reaching out to everyone to book your room reservation.  Stay tuned.</p>\n<strong>FRIDAY</strong>\n3pm &mdash; Guests checkin at Valley View House\n7pm &mdash; Welcome BBQ in the Barn\n9pm &mdash; Campfire\n10pm &mdash; After party: Talent show &amp; rock star karaoke in the Performance Space\n\n<strong>SATURDAY</strong>\n8:30–10:30am &mdash; Breakfast in the Cafe\n11am &mdash; Yoga\n12:30–2pm &mdash; Lunch in the Cafe\n2pm &mdash; Kickball Game in the Middle Field\n5pm &mdash; We get married in the Lower Grove!\n6:30pm &mdash; Cocktail Hour/Taco Bar on the Front Lawn\n7:30-11:30pm &mdash; PARTY!! In the Reception Tent\n11:30pm &mdash; After party in the Performance Space\n1:30am &mdash; After-After party in the Billiards Room\n\nSunday\n9:30am Farewell breakfast in the Cafe\n11am Checkout', 'Itinerary', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', '193-autosave-v1', '', '', '2015-02-03 19:17:01', '2015-02-03 19:17:01', '', 193, 'http://scottyandallie.com/2015/02/03/193-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(255, 3, '2015-02-03 19:21:27', '2015-02-03 19:21:27', 'The most awesome band ETURNITY is playing the wedding!! This 12 piece ensemble is absolutely unreal. <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"http://www.eturnitybandstar.com/\">Check them out here</a></span>.\r\n\r\nFriday night, we\'ll have a DJ, talent show and possibly karaoke. Submit song requests &amp; sign up for the talent show:\r\n\r\n[contact-form subject=\'Scott and Allie#039;s Wedding Request Form\'][contact-field label=\'Name\' type=\'name\' required=\'1\'/][contact-field label=\'Comment\' type=\'textarea\' required=\'1\'/][/contact-form]\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'Music', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', '252-autosave-v1', '', '', '2015-02-03 19:21:27', '2015-02-03 19:21:27', '', 252, 'http://scottyandallie.com/2015/02/03/252-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(256, 0, '2015-02-04 00:37:19', '2015-02-04 00:37:19', 'Work bitch\r\nSex you up, color me bad, obvs\r\nCall me maybe\r\nHair shack\r\nWe are the world\r\nNkotb, again obvs\r\nToxic\r\nAy Bay Bay\n<!--more-->\nAUTHOR: Yo momma\nAUTHOR EMAIL: \nAUTHOR URL: \nSUBJECT: Scott and Allie#039;s Wedding Request Form\nIP: 67.84.196.87\nArray\n(\n    [1_Name] =&gt; Yo momma\n    [2_Comment] =&gt; Work bitch\r\nSex you up, color me bad, obvs\r\nCall me maybe\r\nHair shack\r\nWe are the world\r\nNkotb, again obvs\r\nToxic\r\nAy Bay Bay\n)\n', 'Yo momma - 2015-02-04 00:37:19', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', '557445b6cf621d5c231273379c0e3edd', '', '', '2015-02-04 00:37:19', '2015-02-04 00:37:19', '', 252, 'http://scottyandallie.com/?post_type=feedback&p=256', 0, 'feedback', '', 0),
(258, 2, '2015-02-05 23:56:46', '2015-02-05 23:56:46', '<strong>PLEASE NOTE:</strong> <em>There is a music festival happening the same weekend as the wedding -- please give yourself extra time to get there. Also, watch out for speed traps on Route 28 near Woodstock area.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>ADDRESS:</strong> Full Moon Resort, 12 Valley View Road, Big Indian, NY 12410\r\n<strong>Phone:</strong> (845) 254-5117 www.fullmoonresort.com\r\n\r\n<strong>From the New York City area and Points South (~3hrs):</strong> Take the New York State Thruway (87) North to Exit 19 (Kingston). Take Route 28 West (toward Pine Hill.) Travel approximately 30 miles on Route 28 West to Big Indian/Oliverea. Turn left onto County Route 47 (just after a brown sign on Route 28 which says “Oliverea 3 miles”). Proceed 5 miles on Route 47. Full Moon is on the right. You will see signs. Pull down the Full Moon driveway, parking areas should be clearly designated. If you see the entrance for Pine Hill, on your left, you have gone too far.\r\n\r\n<strong>From the Albany area and Points North (~2hrs): </strong>Take New York State Thruway (87) South towards New York City. Get off at Exit 19, Kingston. Take Route 28 West (toward Pine Hill.) Travel approximately 30 miles on Route 28 West to Big Indian/Oliverea. Turn left onto County Route 47 (just after a brown sign on Route 28 which says “Oliverea 3 miles”). Proceed 5 miles on Route 47. Full Moon is on the right. You will see signs. Pull down the Full Moon driveway, parking areas should be clearly designated. If you see the entrance for Pine Hill, on your left, you have gone too far.\r\n\r\n<strong>From Buffalo/Rochester area and Points North West (~4.5hrs-Roch / </strong><strong>5.5hrs-Buff):</strong> Take the New York State Thruway (I-90) East to Exit 39 (Syracuse). Take I-81 South (toward Binghamton.) Travel approximately 75 miles on I-81 South and, near Binghamton, take NY-17E toward New York. Travel approximately 47 miles on NY-17E to Exit 90; RT-30 N (toward Downsville). Merge quickly onto NY-30 / CR-17 / OLD RT-17 (slight Right). Continue to follow NY-30 for about 38 miles (some curves and turns). Turn Right on NY-28 and travel for approximately 16 miles. You will pass Peekamoose Restaurant (on your right), go over a bridge and see a statue of an Indian on your right as you near the resort. After you pass the Indian statue take a sharp right onto County Route 47. Proceed 5 miles on Route 47. Full Moon is on the right. You will see signs. Pull down the Full Moon driveway, parking areas should be clearly designated.\r\n\r\n<strong>From the Boston area and Points North East (~4hrs):</strong> Take Mass Pike West (I-90). Travel approximately 150 miles and merge onto New York State Thruway West (I-87). After about 7miles, merge onto I-87 South towards New York City. Get off at Exit 19, Kingston. Take Route 28 West (toward Pine Hill.) Travel approximately 30 miles on Route 28 West to Big Indian/Oliverea. Turn left onto County Route 47 (just after a brown sign on Route 28 which says “Oliverea 3 miles”). Proceed 5 miles on Route 47. Full Moon is on the right. You will see signs. Pull down the Full Moon driveway, parking areas should be clearly designated. If you see the entrance for Pine Hill, on your left, you have gone too far.', 'Driving Directions', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', 'driving-directions', '', '', '2015-06-01 20:41:40', '2015-06-01 20:41:40', '', 0, 'http://scottyandallie.com/?page_id=258', 0, 'page', '', 0),
(260, 2, '2015-06-01 20:39:41', '2015-06-01 20:39:41', '<strong>PLEASE NOTE:</strong> <em>There is a music festival happening the same weekend as the wedding -- please give yourself extra time to get there. Also, follow the speed limit on Route 28 as it can be a speed trap.</em>\n\n<strong>ADDRESS:</strong> Full Moon Resort, 12 Valley View Road, Big Indian, NY 12410\n<strong>Phone:</strong> (845) 254-5117 www.fullmoonresort.com\n\n<strong>From the New York City area and Points South (~3hrs):</strong> Take the New York State Thruway (87) North to Exit 19 (Kingston). Take Route 28 West (toward Pine Hill.) Travel approximately 30 miles on Route 28 West to Big Indian/Oliverea. Turn left onto County Route 47 (just after a brown sign on Route 28 which says “Oliverea 3 miles”). Proceed 5 miles on Route 47. Full Moon is on the right. You will see signs. Pull down the Full Moon driveway, parking areas should be clearly designated. If you see the entrance for Pine Hill, on your left, you have gone too far.\n\n<strong>From the Albany area and Points North (~2hrs): </strong>Take New York State Thruway (87) South towards New York City. Get off at Exit 19, Kingston. Take Route 28 West (toward Pine Hill.) Travel approximately 30 miles on Route 28 West to Big Indian/Oliverea. Turn left onto County Route 47 (just after a brown sign on Route 28 which says “Oliverea 3 miles”). Proceed 5 miles on Route 47. Full Moon is on the right. You will see signs. Pull down the Full Moon driveway, parking areas should be clearly designated. If you see the entrance for Pine Hill, on your left, you have gone too far.\n\n<strong>From Buffalo/Rochester area and Points North West (~4.5hrs-Roch / </strong><strong>5.5hrs-Buff):</strong> Take the New York State Thruway (I-90) East to Exit 39 (Syracuse). Take I-81 South (toward Binghamton.) Travel approximately 75 miles on I-81 South and, near Binghamton, take NY-17E toward New York. Travel approximately 47 miles on NY-17E to Exit 90; RT-30 N (toward Downsville). Merge quickly onto NY-30 / CR-17 / OLD RT-17 (slight Right). Continue to follow NY-30 for about 38 miles (some curves and turns). Turn Right on NY-28 and travel for approximately 16 miles. You will pass Peekamoose Restaurant (on your right), go over a bridge and see a statue of an Indian on your right as you near the resort. After you pass the Indian statue take a sharp right onto County Route 47. Proceed 5 miles on Route 47. Full Moon is on the right. You will see signs. Pull down the Full Moon driveway, parking areas should be clearly designated.\n\n<strong>From the Boston area and Points North East (~4hrs):</strong> Take Mass Pike West (I-90). Travel approximately 150 miles and merge onto New York State Thruway West (I-87). After about 7miles, merge onto I-87 South towards New York City. Get off at Exit 19, Kingston. Take Route 28 West (toward Pine Hill.) Travel approximately 30 miles on Route 28 West to Big Indian/Oliverea. Turn left onto County Route 47 (just after a brown sign on Route 28 which says “Oliverea 3 miles”). Proceed 5 miles on Route 47. Full Moon is on the right. You will see signs. Pull down the Full Moon driveway, parking areas should be clearly designated. If you see the entrance for Pine Hill, on your left, you have gone too far.', 'Driving Directions', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', '258-autosave-v1', '', '', '2015-06-01 20:39:41', '2015-06-01 20:39:41', '', 258, 'http://scottyandallie.com/2015/02/07/258-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
